            <p>Our customers LOVE their shark diving photos. Divers that book photos get extra attention and guidance from their  photographer who is also a highly experienced and highly trained shark diver and water safety expert. Adding a photos to your dive means that you'll have a professional photographer and diver guiding you to get the best experience and the best shots possible and with a once in a lifetime experience like cage-free shark diving with one of the best crews in the business, you'll definitely want to add some photos to your experience.</p>
            <p>You can tell people about your experience, but people simply wont understand the true value of what you've experienced without seeing the photos. Not only that, but you'll have the photographic evidence to proove what you did and to remembrer and share for the rest of your life.</p>
            <p>Our only advice is to not wait until the last minute to add photos to your tour. Our photographers are in high demand and we only have a limited number of photographers available for each tour. If you want photos, we recommend adding them to your tour at the time of booking.</p>
            <p>Finally, remember to really soak in the experience and enjoy your time with the sharks. Our photographers will be there to capture the moments, but don't forget to take a moment to just enjoy the experience and the beauty of Hawaii's ocean and wildlife. There will likely be a lot going on when you're in the water and it's easy to get caught up in the excitement of trying to get the perfect shots and end up missing out on the actual experience of really being there with these incredible creatures in the open ocean.</p>
